# Claims
```json
[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/gates/github-actions.ts",
  "line": 179,
  "title": "Separate dispatch intent from dispatch sent, and bound discovery of a run that may not exist",
  "detail": "Thank you: review confirmed the trust boundary.\n- Dispatch comes from the default branch's SHA, and a candidate's CI-file changes are refused before push.\n- Commands come from the trusted gate configuration.\n- The workflow is dispatch-only with `contents: read`: no secrets, no credential persistence, pinned actions, no cache, no input interpolation.\n- ETag polling, fail-closed handling of missing and incomplete jobs, and redaction before clipping.\nSix of the seven earlier required cases are covered.\n\nRestart defects, all reproduced:\n(1) `dispatchSent=true` is persisted before the POST (~179). A crash between the two makes the restart skip dispatch and poll discovery without bound (~209) for a run that never existed. Persist `dispatchIntent` before the POST and `dispatchSent` after it is accepted. On restart with intent but not sent, look for the run for a bounded time (a stated visibility deadline). If it isn't found, dispatch once more under the same handle. If the outcome is still uncertain, fail the check with a clear reason instead of polling forever."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/pipeline/gate-execution.ts",
  "line": 147,
  "title": "Persist the completed result before releasing the execution handle",
  "detail": "The handle is cleared and saved (~147) before the caller records the gate results in `lastGates` (engine.ts ~1727). Review reproduced, with the real Store, a crash between those two checkpoints that restarted the same SHA, stage, round and purpose with a new handle and dispatched twice. Save the completed result durably with the handle (or in the same save as `lastGates`) before relinquishing the execution identity, and on restart reuse the stored completion."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
  "file": "src/gates/github-actions.ts",
  "line": 76,
  "title": "Delete the trusted branches only after cancellation or completion is confirmed",
  "detail": "Cleanup treats an exhausted visibility deadline as a successful discovery cleanup (~76), and goes on deleting both branches when cancellation throws (~85-91). An accepted but invisible workflow can then keep running while cleanup reports success and the pipeline clears its handle. Both cases were reproduced. Keep the branches and a durable cleanup obligation until cancellation or completion is confirmed, and retry cleanup on the next tick or restart. The existing test at gates-github-actions.test.ts ~675 expects deletion after a failed cancellation: change it."
 },
 {
  "id": "F4",
  "file": "src/gates/github-actions.ts",
  "line": 139,
  "title": "Wait out rate limits on polls instead of cancelling the gate",
  "detail": "A single HTTP 429 or secondary-rate-limit response on the run or job poll (~139) rejects straight into discard (~259) and cancels an active gate. Review reproduced it with an injected 429. Honour `Retry-After` or the reset time with a bounded wait, under one deadline shared with the check's timeout, and keep the execution identity throughout. Only a non-retryable error or the deadline fails the check.\n\nAdd these regression tests from review (they fail on this PR; adjust helpers as needed, don't weaken them):\n\n```ts\ntest(\"review regression: failed cancellation preserves branches for cleanup retry\", async () => {\n  const f = fixture();\n  f.state.runStatus = \"in_progress\";\n  const h = await f.stored({ dispatchSent: true, runId: 17 });\n  const gh = f.deps.gh;\n  f.deps.gh = async (...args) => {\n    if (args[0][1]?.endsWith(\"/cancel\")) throw new Error(\"cancel unavailable\");\n    return (await gh(...args)) ?? \"\";\n  };\n  await expect(f.executor().discard?.(h)).rejects.toThrow(\"cancel unavailable\");\n  expect(f.calls.filter((call) => call.startsWith(\"delete:\"))).toEqual([]);\n  expect(f.remote.size).toBe(2);\n});\n\ntest(\"review regression: invisible accepted dispatch is not declared cleaned up\", async () => {\n  const f = fixture();\n  f.state.visibleAfter = Infinity;\n  f.state.runStatus = \"in_progress\";\n  const h = await f.stored({ dispatchSent: true });\n  await expect(f.executor().discard?.(h)).rejects.toThrow();\n  expect(f.calls.filter((call) => call.startsWith(\"delete:\"))).toEqual([]);\n});\n\ntest(\"review regression: persisted intent without a visible dispatch has a bounded discovery failure\", async () => {\n  const f = fixture();\n  f.state.visibleAfter = Infinity;\n  // This is the durable state after saving intent but before sending the POST.\n  const h = await f.stored({ dispatchSent: true });\n  await expect(f.run(signal(), h)).rejects.toThrow(\n    /dispatch.*(?:unknown|unconfirmed|not observed)|discovery.*(?:deadline|timed out)/i,\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"review regression: completion survives restart before the caller saves gate results\", async () => {\n  const f = fixture();\n  const { ctx, store } = await context(f);\n  try {\n    const push = f.deps.push;\n    f.deps.push = async (p) => {\n      const durable = store.getRunState<RunState>(ctx.run.id)?.gateExecution?.handle;\n      if (durable) f.saved.push(durable);\n      await push(p);\n    };\n    await runGateExecution(ctx, \"gates\", \"initial\", cwd, req.gates);\n    // The engine has not yet stored lastGates/baseline or completed the stage.\n    const restarted = new RunContext(ctx.deps, ctx.run, ctx.repo, signal());\n    await runGateExecution(restarted, \"gates\", \"initial\", cwd, req.gates);\n    expect(f.calls.filter((call) => call === \"dispatch\")).toHaveLength(1);\n  } finally {\n    store.close();\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"review regression: a temporary poll rate limit does not cancel the gate\", async () => {\n  const f = fixture();\n  f.state.runStatus = \"in_progress\";\n  f.state.onSleep = () => {\n    f.state.runStatus = \"completed\";\n  };\n  const gh = f.deps.gh;\n  let limited = false;\n  f.deps.gh = async (...args) => {\n    if (!limited && args[0].includes(\"--include\")) {\n      limited = true;\n      throw new Error(\"HTTP 429: secondary rate limit; Retry-After: 1\");\n    }\n    return (await gh(...args)) ?? \"\";\n  };\n  await expect(f.run()).resolves.toMatchObject({ setupOk: true });\n  expect(f.calls).not.toContain(\"cancel\");\n});\n```"
 },
